# 13\. BACKEND ARCHITECTURE

Build a modular Express API.

All endpoints must use:

/api/v1

Response format:

{ "success": true, "data": {}, "error": null }

For errors:

{ "success": false, "data": null, "error": { "code": "VALIDATION\_ERROR", "message": "Invalid request" } }

Implement the following routes.

### Video

POST /api/v1/video/parse

Input: { "url": "[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=](<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=>)..." }

Output: { "videoId": "..." }

### Transcript

GET /api/v1/transcript/:videoId

Output: { "lines": \[ { "id": "line-1", "start": 0, "end": 3, "text": "Example sentence", "language": "en" } \] }

### Translation

POST /api/v1/translate

Input: { "text": "Hello", "targetLang": "fr" }

Output: { "translated": "Bonjour" }

### Suggestions

GET /api/v1/suggestions

### User limits

GET /api/v1/user/limits

### Authentication

POST /api/v1/auth/login

### Health

GET /api/v1/health

### Additional backend requirements

- Route/controller/service separation.
- Zod request validation.
- Centralized error handling.
- CORS restrictions.
- Environment variable validation.
- Request rate limiting.
- Structured logging.
- Consistent response types.
- Appropriate HTTP status codes.

Never expose API keys to the frontend.

