## My recommendation for using this prompt

If you're using an autonomous coding agent, don't ask it to generate everything in one shot without checking its work.

Use this execution sequence:

1. Architecture and foundation
   Ask the agent to inspect your project, establish the architecture, and configure the frontend and backend.
2. Core learning experience
   Focus on the video player, transcript, synchronization, translations, and customization.
3. SaaS functionality
   Implement subscriptions, usage limits, authentication mock, pricing, and settings.
4. Backend integration
   Connect all frontend features to the API and implement mock providers.
5. Testing and refinement
   Ask the agent to run the application, test every interaction, fix errors, and polish the UI.

One final suggestion: Make the transcript experience your biggest competitive advantage. A particularly valuable future feature would be interactive word-level learning: users click any word in a transcript sentence to see its definition, pronunciation, translation, and example usage. This could eventually make LinguaTube much more than a YouTube transcript viewer.
